WEBVTT

1
00:52:28.290 --> 00:52:31.530
Today people here for the first time, we have guests present today.

2
00:52:31.530 --> 00:52:38.490
Give a wave if you are here for the first time, for the first time, people for the very first time.

3
00:52:38.490 --> 00:52:42.170
No guests? Bad news, but well.

4
00:52:42.170 --> 00:52:49.890
May I have a round of applause for our guests? You are very welcome, super nice.

5
00:52:49.890 --> 00:52:53.490
Welcome to Open Church.

6
00:52:53.490 --> 00:52:59.490
And I apologize if we sometimes act a bit strange.

7
00:52:59.490 --> 00:53:07.490
I do feel sorry, but I don't regret it at all. Hallelujah.

8
00:53:07.490 --> 00:53:16.090
Starting next week, starting next week we step into the Easter month.

9
00:53:16.090 --> 00:53:19.290
At least, that's how I want to celebrate it for myself.

10
00:53:19.290 --> 00:53:28.290
I want to celebrate throughout the whole month of March what Jesus has done for us. Amen.

11
00:53:28.290 --> 00:53:33.090
What has He done for us? Jesus is God Himself.

12
00:53:33.090 --> 00:53:39.090
Let me sketch one paragraph full of what the good message is for our faith.

13
00:53:39.090 --> 00:53:44.290
Jesus is God Himself, Creator of heaven and earth.

14
00:53:44.290 --> 00:53:54.490
He made everything and to Him belongs all glory and honor forever for who He is.

15
00:53:54.490 --> 00:53:59.090
God deserves all glory and honor, I can sign up for that.

16
00:53:59.090 --> 00:54:09.290
And this God, to whom all glory and honor belongs, chose to become a man, lower than the angels.

17
00:54:09.290 --> 00:54:14.690
And He became man to become sinful through my sin.

18
00:54:14.690 --> 00:54:17.690
He committed no sin, I committed sin.

19
00:54:17.690 --> 00:54:24.690
And instead of me having to die and be condemned and live in distance from the Father,

20
00:54:24.690 --> 00:54:31.290
Jesus God Himself chose to become man and take my guilt upon Himself.

21
00:54:31.290 --> 00:54:35.090
Glory to the name of Jesus.

22
00:54:35.090 --> 00:54:46.290
And to never forget this and to let it take root deeply in our faith, in our belief, in our hearts,

23
00:54:46.290 --> 00:54:49.890
that it will always continue to bear fruit.

24
00:54:49.890 --> 00:54:56.890
I do not want to forget this, church. I want, I want this to keep growing.

25
00:54:56.890 --> 00:54:59.690
I do not want to forget what Jesus has done for me.

26
00:54:59.890 --> 00:55:06.290
I do not want there to ever be a moment when I stood in the baptismal water and oh hallelujah, thank you Jesus.

27
00:55:06.290 --> 00:55:10.090
And that I was happy then, but over the years it fades away.

28
00:55:10.090 --> 00:55:14.490
No, I do not want that. I do not want it to fade, I want it to get better.

29
00:55:14.490 --> 00:55:18.490
I want it to increase. Do you understand what I mean?

30
00:55:18.690 --> 00:55:30.290
And so during the Easter month, we will simply talk about who Jesus is and what He has done in Open Church.

31
00:55:30.290 --> 00:55:36.090
We will go into the gospels, the four gospels, Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John,

32
00:55:36.090 --> 00:55:45.290
we will talk about who Jesus is and what His mission was and what He did and why He did what He did.

33
00:55:45.290 --> 00:55:54.090
What He ultimately did. He healed people, He provided food, but there is one ultimate act that He has done.

34
00:55:54.090 --> 00:55:57.090
And that is dying for the sin of humanity.

35
00:55:57.090 --> 00:56:03.290
But He rose from the dead, for we have a living God. Amen. We have a living God.

36
00:56:03.290 --> 00:56:13.890
I myself, on a personal note, have decided to fast this year during the Easter weekend on Good Friday, Saturday, and Sunday.

37
00:56:13.890 --> 00:56:20.490
Because I caught myself a few years ago on Good Friday.

38
00:56:20.490 --> 00:56:26.690
Seriously, I caught myself that it was Good Friday. Suddenly it was Good Friday.

39
00:56:26.690 --> 00:56:30.890
Oh, it is Good Friday. Society in the Netherlands just goes on.

40
00:56:30.890 --> 00:56:34.490
People just work on that day. It is just a normal day.

41
00:56:34.490 --> 00:56:40.290
And I caught myself thinking wow, this is the day my Lord died.

42
00:56:40.290 --> 00:56:45.290
I want to experience that day. I want that day, oh yes, it is Good Friday.

43
00:56:45.290 --> 00:56:48.090
Yes, are you doing anything on Good Friday? Ah yes, it is Good Friday.

44
00:56:48.090 --> 00:56:53.890
I want to experience that day, because it is a day of victory and it is a deep day.

45
00:56:53.890 --> 00:57:01.690
And so I have chosen to not eat anything all day this Good Friday, only water.

46
00:57:01.690 --> 00:57:06.090
Then you have Saturday, then I also eat nothing, only water.

47
00:57:06.090 --> 00:57:09.290
And Sunday morning nothing until the service, only water.

48
00:57:09.290 --> 00:57:13.090
And then Sunday afternoon I will go all out. Amen.

49
00:57:13.090 --> 00:57:16.090
To celebrate that we have a risen Lord.

50
00:57:16.090 --> 00:57:20.290
But I want to experience this Easter weekend.

51
00:57:20.290 --> 00:57:26.890
I know from myself that when I am fasting, I don't feel so happy physically,

52
00:57:26.890 --> 00:57:30.090
but every word I read from Scripture comes alive twice as well.

53
00:57:30.090 --> 00:57:32.090
I don't know if you have ever experienced that too.

54
00:57:32.090 --> 00:57:35.090
And that is what I want to experience this Easter.

55
00:57:35.090 --> 00:57:39.090
Often, I want to celebrate Good Friday.

56
00:57:39.090 --> 00:57:41.090
Celebrating in his death.

57
00:57:41.090 --> 00:57:46.090
Paul literally says in the book of Corinthians that you must celebrate his death.

58
00:57:46.090 --> 00:57:49.090
That is very strange, that is very contradictory, but it must be so.

59
00:57:49.090 --> 00:57:52.090
And I want to invite you to join me.

60
00:57:52.090 --> 00:57:54.090
Then you have to decide for yourself how you do it.

61
00:57:54.090 --> 00:57:55.090
I'm not even going to ask about it.

62
00:57:55.090 --> 00:57:57.090
I'm not going to cheer you on with my eyes.

63
00:57:57.090 --> 00:57:59.090
We should never do that as a church.

64
00:57:59.090 --> 00:58:01.090
Fasting is something very personal.

65
00:58:01.090 --> 00:58:02.090
That's something you do yourself.

66
00:58:02.090 --> 00:58:05.090
Some people then say okay, on Good Friday, now that you've heard that,

67
00:58:05.090 --> 00:58:07.090
I might skip meat.

68
00:58:07.090 --> 00:58:09.090
Or I won't eat cookies.

69
00:58:09.090 --> 00:58:12.090
Or that day I won't use social media.

70
00:58:12.090 --> 00:58:16.090
But well, fasting according to the Bible is not eating.

71
00:58:16.090 --> 00:58:17.090
Right?

72
00:58:17.090 --> 00:58:19.090
But of course, you can take steps in that.

73
00:58:19.090 --> 00:58:24.090
But I want to invite you to be intensely focused on Jesus during this upcoming Easter month,

74
00:58:24.090 --> 00:58:26.090
We can go through all the Bible stories from the whole Bible

75
00:58:26.090 --> 00:58:30.090
and in Noah we can see Christ, of course.

76
00:58:30.090 --> 00:58:33.090
But let's focus solely on the Son of God during the Easter month.

77
00:58:33.090 --> 00:58:39.090
Is that a good agreement?

78
00:58:39.090 --> 00:58:40.090
Hallelujah.

79
00:58:40.090 --> 00:58:41.090
Praise is good.

80
00:58:41.090 --> 00:58:42.090


81
00:58:42.090 --> 00:58:47.090
Chris, I would like to invite you to this wonderful stage.

82
00:58:51.090 --> 00:58:52.090
Just a little cover on it.

83
00:58:54.090 --> 00:58:55.090
Hallelujah.

84
00:58:55.090 --> 00:58:56.090
God is so good.

85
00:58:56.090 --> 00:58:57.090
God is so good.

86
00:58:59.090 --> 00:59:04.090
This morning I want to talk about the eternal value of returning.

87
00:59:05.090 --> 00:59:06.090
Ouch, what was that?

88
00:59:06.090 --> 00:59:07.090
Well, I will explain that.

89
00:59:09.090 --> 00:59:13.090
If you look, Ecclesiastes says, everything is just air and emptiness, says Ecclesiastes.

90
00:59:13.090 --> 00:59:15.090
Nothing really makes sense.

91
00:59:15.090 --> 00:59:18.090
All of life is just air and something incomprehensible.

92
00:59:20.090 --> 00:59:22.090
And then we also have James, who says something similar.

93
00:59:22.090 --> 00:59:27.090
But you do not even know what your life will look like tomorrow.

94
00:59:27.090 --> 00:59:30.090
For a person is like a mist cloud.

95
00:59:30.090 --> 00:59:33.090
For a little while it is there and then it is gone again.

96
00:59:34.090 --> 00:59:40.090
A Kempish Bible translation would say, the life of a person on earth flies by like a fart.

97
00:59:41.090 --> 00:59:45.090
One a silent killer, the other a lot of noise without real content.

98
00:59:47.090 --> 00:59:48.090
And everything in between.

99
00:59:49.090 --> 00:59:52.090
I find it very important to make this very clear.

100
00:59:52.090 --> 00:59:55.090
For now comes the other side, the Jews used to do that too.

101
00:59:56.090 --> 00:59:57.090
They love contradictions.

102
00:59:58.090 --> 01:00:03.090
For without Jesus we are indeed perishable and life is elusive.

103
01:00:04.090 --> 01:00:05.090
That is true.

104
01:00:05.090 --> 01:00:08.090
But in Jesus we are meant for eternity.

105
01:00:10.090 --> 01:00:15.090
And that applies to everything in who we may be for Him and what we may do for Him.

106
01:00:15.090 --> 01:00:20.090
And this morning I want to convey that eternal perspective in the act of bringing back.

107
01:00:21.090 --> 01:00:25.090
And I want to show it, for it is about the promise that the Father has made to us.

108
01:00:26.090 --> 01:00:27.090
The promise.

109
01:00:28.090 --> 01:00:33.090
For God Himself has said in today's text, I do not know if that could be projected.

110
01:00:34.090 --> 01:00:38.090
The Father says, I will always keep my covenant.

111
01:00:39.090 --> 01:00:41.090
I will not break my promise.

112
01:00:41.090 --> 01:00:43.090
I will not break my promise.

113
01:00:44.090 --> 01:00:46.090
God is a covenant God.

114
01:00:47.090 --> 01:00:49.090
And He speaks in this text about David.

115
01:00:50.090 --> 01:00:54.090
But in Jesus the Father says this about us as well.

116
01:00:55.090 --> 01:00:58.090
For in Jesus we are children of the promise.

117
01:00:59.090 --> 01:01:00.090
And of His covenant.

118
01:01:01.090 --> 01:01:07.090
And that makes it important for the Father, that as we bring back in obedience and joy.

119
01:01:08.090 --> 01:01:12.090
For in that way we participate in His promise.

120
01:01:13.090 --> 01:01:14.090
And we participate in His covenant.

121
01:01:15.090 --> 01:01:19.090
But do we also participate in his intention with who we may be in him.

122
01:01:20.090 --> 01:01:23.090
It shows that we may trust in him.

123
01:01:24.090 --> 01:01:25.090
And that we believe in him.

124
01:01:26.090 --> 01:01:28.090
But it also truly shows that we do that.

125
01:01:29.090 --> 01:01:37.090
And he is such that he has given his great promise.

126
01:01:38.090 --> 01:01:42.090
And we actually also show that we believe that he will fulfill that promise.

127
01:01:43.090 --> 01:01:45.090
So we trust him to fulfill that promise.

128
01:01:46.090 --> 01:01:47.090
That is important to him.

129
01:01:48.090 --> 01:01:50.090
And also all the accompanying promise.

130
01:01:52.090 --> 01:01:55.090
The Father finds it wonderful, he truly finds it wonderful.

131
01:01:55.090 --> 01:01:58.090
When we believe in him and when we do what he says.

132
01:01:59.090 --> 01:02:02.090
Returning is like a sacrifice, like a gift for him.

133
01:02:03.090 --> 01:02:05.090
And this has eternal value for him.

134
01:02:06.090 --> 01:02:08.090
Just like worship and prayer, it is actually also worship.

135
01:02:09.090 --> 01:02:10.090
A form of it.

136
01:02:11.090 --> 01:02:13.090
It is building his heavenly household.

137
01:02:14.090 --> 01:02:15.090
As living stones.

138
01:02:16.090 --> 01:02:20.090
It means that our life and giving do not have to pass by like a fleeting moment.

139
01:02:20.090 --> 01:02:25.090
But our life and giving is meant to be a living stone in his house forever.

140
01:02:26.090 --> 01:02:28.090
And an eternally pleasing fragrance for the Father.

141
01:02:29.090 --> 01:02:32.090
To make him happy for what he will reward us for.

142
01:02:33.090 --> 01:02:35.090
And he has simply promised that.

143
01:02:36.090 --> 01:02:37.090
This is also what he wants.

144
01:02:38.090 --> 01:02:39.090
He wants to be together with us, he wants togetherness.

145
01:02:40.090 --> 01:02:42.090
And this togetherness is so important that we bring it back together.

146
01:02:43.090 --> 01:02:44.090
That we show it together.

147
01:02:45.090 --> 01:02:46.090
But what God has said, that is true.

148
01:02:47.090 --> 01:02:48.090
And that will come to pass.

149
01:02:48.090 --> 01:02:51.090
And that we make a covenant decision.

150
01:02:52.090 --> 01:02:53.090
And that we make him happy today.

151
01:02:54.090 --> 01:02:55.090
And I want to bless us in this.

152
01:02:56.090 --> 01:02:59.090
And I would also say a lot of blessings as you return today.

153
01:03:00.090 --> 01:03:01.090
In Jesus' name.

154
01:03:14.090 --> 01:03:15.090
Good morning.

155
01:03:16.090 --> 01:03:17.090
Good morning.

